## Method and reasoning
For current prefix sum s, a prior prefix contributes exactly when it equals s−K. Start the frequency table with one occurrence of zero. Count before inserting s so an empty interval is never counted. Both the prefix and the answer need 64 bits.

## Walk through the sample
The sample prefixes are 0, 1, 0, 0, −1, 0, including the initial zero. For K = 0, choose two equal prefixes. The four zeros contribute 4 × 3 / 2 = 6 intervals.

## Complexity
Expected time O(n), space O(n).

## Reference implementation
~~~
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);
    int n;
    long long k;
    cin >> n >> k;
    unordered_map<long long, int> count;
    count.reserve(2 * n + 1);
    count[0] = 1;
    long long prefix = 0, answer = 0;
    while (n--) {
        long long x;
        cin >> x;
        prefix += x;
        auto it = count.find(prefix - k);
        if (it != count.end())
            answer += it->second;
        ++count[prefix];
    }
    cout << answer << '\n';
}
~~~
